# Optional: "save to your own storage" accounts. See docs/ACCOUNT-SYNC.md.
# These are public client ids, not secrets. The feature has no client secret
# anywhere by design, because a static export cannot keep one.
# Leave them unset and the app works exactly as before, minus cloud saving.

# Google Drive, web build. Authorized origins must include the deployed site
# and http://localhost:9002 for dev.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# Google Drive, Tauri desktop build (a "Desktop app" OAuth client). Required
# for desktop sign-in: the web id above cannot stand in, because Google rejects
# a 127.0.0.1 redirect on a Web client.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_DESKTOP_CLIENT_ID=

# The matching secret for that Desktop-app client. Google's token endpoint
# demands it even with PKCE, and Google's own installed-app docs ship it inside
# the binary, so this is the one "secret" here and it is not a real one. Never
# put a Web client's secret in this file: that one is genuinely confidential.
# This is the "Client secret" field, NOT the id above. It looks like
# GOCSPX-xxxxxxxx and never ends in .apps.googleusercontent.com; copying the id
# here fails the sign-in only after the consent screen.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_DESKTOP_CLIENT_SECRET=

# GitHub gists, desktop device flow only (no secret needed).
NEXT_PUBLIC_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=

# GitHub sign-in Worker, which turns the web GitHub option into a real login
# button. Deploy workers/github-oauth and put its URL here. Leave it unset and
# the web build asks the user to paste a personal access token instead.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GITHUB_OAUTH_PROXY=

# Translation API Servers
# Defaults to trybooks.org (primary) and ludowala.app (fallback) if unset.
NEXT_PUBLIC_TRANSLATION_PRIMARY_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_TRANSLATION_FALLBACK_URL=

# The PocketBase backend in infra/vps. One URL, two features:
#
#   the community feed (Discover)  the posts people share, and the comments,
#                                  likes and follows on them
#   cloud projects                 saving the editable project to that box, so
#                                  it can be reopened on another device or
#                                  handed to somebody as a link
#
# Point this at the box and both turn on; leave it unset and both disappear from
# the editor entirely — no rail button, no Community tab, no Save to cloud — and
# everything else works exactly as before. Saving to storage the user owns
# (Drive, GitHub gists) is independent of this and always available.
#
# Public by definition: it is the hostname every visitor's browser connects to.
# There is no key here and there is not meant to be one. Reading the feed needs
# no credential at all; writing to it, and everything to do with a cloud project,
# needs a session minted from the Google or GitHub sign-in the editor already
# has, which is verified server side.
#
#   local docker:  http://127.0.0.1:8090
#   production:    https://pb.openscrgen.app
NEXT_PUBLIC_DISCOVER_URL=

# The MCP relay, which lets Claude Code, Claude Desktop, Cursor or VS Code drive
# the editor in a browser. The desktop app needs none of this: it hosts its own
# MCP server on 127.0.0.1, because a native process can open a socket and a
# browser tab cannot. Deploy infra/vps/mcp-relay and put its URL here; leave it
# unset and the web build has no MCP feature at all, no pill and no dialog.
#
# Public by definition, and not a credential: the relay holds no secret and can
# reach no tab on its own. What identifies a tab is a random code the browser
# generates and shows you, which you paste into your AI client.
#
#   local docker:  http://127.0.0.1:8722
#   production:    https://mcp.openscrgen.app
NEXT_PUBLIC_MCP_RELAY_URL=

# Live editing: where the signalling server is (the mcp-relay container hosts
# it, so this is normally the same URL as NEXT_PUBLIC_MCP_RELAY_URL and can be
# left unset when that is set). Unset and unavailable = no invite link, no
# sessions, and the editor is exactly what it was.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_COLLAB_URL=https://mcp.example.com

# Live editing: expiring TURN credentials, for the pairs whose networks refuse a
# direct connection. Point it at an endpoint that mints them from a coturn
# shared secret (the secret itself must never be in a NEXT_PUBLIC_ value: every
# one of them is inlined into the bundle). Unset = STUN only, which still
# connects most pairs.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TURN_ENDPOINT=https://example.com/api/turn

# Live editing: STUN, which only tells a browser its own public address.
# Comma separated. Defaults to Google's public server.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_STUN_URLS=stun:stun.example.com:3478
